The older Pade driver gives the right finite cover: branch on the first nonzero reciprocal coefficient `F_r`, set earlier `F_i=0`, normalize `F_r=1`, solve the tail coefficients of `F^(3/2)`, and invert the next coefficient. This branches on a proven nonzero variable instead of choosing one by wish. I’m testing those branch systems directly.
